Slope check: for consecutive union times a<b: slopeSum = Σ_curve slope of curve on [a,b]. Each curve either doesn't span (contributes 0) or [a,b] within one of its segments (since union includes its nodes) → slope = (f2-f1)/(t2-t1) rational. |slopeSum| ≤ maxRamp.

Rat class:
```java
private static final class Rat {
    private BigDecimal num = BigDecimal.ZERO;
    private BigDecimal den = BigDecimal.ONE;

    void add(BigDecimal n, BigDecimal d) {
        num = num.multiply(d).add(n.multiply(den));
        den = den.multiply(d);
    }

    int compareTo(BigDecimal limit) {
        return num.compareTo(limit.multiply(den));
    }

    Rat negated? for abs: compare |sum| ≤ limit ⟺ -limit ≤ sum ≤ limit → two compares: num ≤ limit*den && num ≥ -limit*den.
}
```

Interpolation at time t within curve: binary search segment. Curve nodes sorted. If t < first or t > last → skip. If t equals a node → that flow (still fine via segment formula). Find i such that nodes[i].minute <= t <= nodes[i+1].minute: num = f_i*(t_{i+1}-t) + f_{i+1}*(t-t_i), den = (t_{i+1}-t_i). Check: linear interpolation f(t) = f_i + (f_{i+1}-f_i)*(t-t_i)/(t_{i+1}-t_i) = [f_i*(t_{i+1}-t_i) + (f_{i+1}-f_i)*(t-t_i)]/(t_{i+1}-t_i) = [f_i*(t_{i+1}-t) + f_{i+1}*(t-t_i)]/(t_{i+1}-t_i). ✓

Slope on [a,b] for curve: if b <= first or a >= last → 0. Else find segment containing a (nodes[i].minute <= a < nodes[i+1].minute; since a,b are union points and curve nodes ⊆ union, b <= nodes[i+1].minute). slope num = f_{i+1}-f_i, den = t_{i+1}-t_i.

